📊 Dashboard Walkthrough

📄 Page 1 - Executive Overview

This page provides a high-level summary of the business using key performance indicators (KPIs) such as total orders, total customers, total revenue, and overall business performance trends.

📄 Page 2 - Detail Analysis

This page provides a detailed analysis of business performance by allowing deeper exploration of sales patterns, customer activity, and operational trends.

📄 Page 3 - Sales & Category Analysis

This page analyzes sales performance across different product categories, identifies top-performing categories, and highlights revenue distribution.

📄 Page 4 - Customer Reviews

This page evaluates customer satisfaction by analyzing ratings, review patterns, and identifying areas with higher customer complaints.

📄 Page 5 - Delivery Operations

This page monitors delivery efficiency, tracks delivery delays, and identifies regions that require operational improvements.

📄 Page 6 - Seller & Geography

This page analyzes seller performance and visualizes the geographical distribution of sales to understand regional business performance.

📄 Page 7 - Payment Behavior

This page studies customer payment preferences, compares payment methods, and identifies payment behavior trends.

💼 Management Recommendations
1. Improve delivery operations in delayed regions

Focus on optimizing logistics and partnering with efficient delivery providers in regions with higher delivery times to improve customer satisfaction.

2. Promote digital payment adoption

Encourage customers to use digital payment methods by offering discounts, cashback, or reward points to reduce dependency on Cash on Delivery (COD).

3. Strengthen customer retention strategies

Introduce loyalty programs, personalized offers, and targeted campaigns to increase repeat purchases and improve customer lifetime value.

4. Diversify the seller network

Onboard more sellers and support underperforming sellers to reduce dependency on a small group of high-performing sellers.

5. Improve product quality and customer experience

Monitor low-rated products, improve quality checks, and address customer complaints to increase customer satisfaction and reduce negative reviews.

# Data Limitations

1. The dashboard analysis is based on the available historical e-commerce dataset and may not represent current business performance.

2. The analysis does not use real-time data; therefore, the insights may change if new transactions are added.

3. Some dashboard findings may be affected by missing, incomplete, or inconsistent values present in the original dataset.

4. External factors such as festivals, promotional campaigns, seasonal demand, and economic conditions were not included in this analysis.

5. Customer behavior, payment preferences, and delivery patterns can change over time, so the results should be interpreted accordingly.

6. The dashboard focuses only on the provided e-commerce data and does not include additional business information such as inventory, marketing, or customer support data.

# Improvement List

1. Integrate real-time data sources to keep the dashboard updated automatically.

2. Add forecasting visuals to predict future sales trends and customer demand.

3. Include customer segmentation analysis to better understand customer groups and purchasing behavior.

4. Develop advanced seller performance KPIs for deeper seller evaluation.

5. Add region-wise profitability analysis to identify high-performing and low-performing areas.

6. Expand the dashboard by incorporating marketing, inventory, and customer support data for a more comprehensive business view.
